>> title: Corned Beef, Slow Cooker
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: beef, cured, brisket, slow cooker, crock pot, deli
>> counters: The Slow Cooker
>> dish: corned-beef
>> kit: Slow Cooker
>> aka: corned beef brisket, salt beef, boiled beef, corn beef, brined brisket, slow cooker corned beef, crockpot corned beef
>> pairs-with: pastrami, sauerkraut, russian-dressing, deli-rye-bread
>> servings: 6
>> time: 5 days 12 hr 20 min
>> slack: narrow — the cabbage has about an hour; left in for three it goes grey and sulphurous and the whole pot tastes of it
>> washing-up: the slow cooker crock, the non-reactive tub, a bowl to soak the brisket in

Nothing is browned and nothing should be. A cured brisket is simmered and never seared.

>> step: stir the brine
Stir @water{4%L}(1 gal, cold), @kosher salt{200%g}(1 cup Diamond Crystal), @dark brown sugar{100%g}(1/2 cup packed), @pink curing salt{25%g}(5 tsp; cure #1), @pickling spice{4%Tbs} and @garlic{10%cloves}(crushed) until the salt and sugar have gone.

>> step: brine 5 days, turn daily
Submerge @beef brisket{4%lb}(1.8 kg, flat cut; halved crosswise if it will not lie flat in the crock) in @&(~1)brine{} in a #non-reactive tub{}, weight it under the surface, and ~brine{5%days} in the fridge, turning it over once a day.

>> step: rinse, soak 2 hr
Rinse @&(~1)cured brisket{} and ~soak{2%hr} in @cold water{4%L}(1 gal, changed once).

>> step: simmer on low, 9 hr
Slow cook @&(~1)soaked brisket{} in a #slow cooker{} on low for ~slow cook{9%hr} with @water{2%qt}(1.9 L; to barely cover), @yellow onion{1%large}(halved), @carrots{2}(cut in 2-in lengths), @bay leaves{2} and @black peppercorns{1%tsp}.

>> step: add the cabbage for the last hour, then rest 20 min
Add @green cabbage{1%small}(cut in 6 wedges through the core) to @&(~1)pot{} for a further ~slow cook{60%min}, then lift the brisket out, ~rest{20%min} under foil, and carve it across the grain, which turns ninety degrees partway along the flat.
